<P>
  Two unusual things happened that day. I was riding a ski lift, and a kid said
  something that stuck with me.
</P>
<P>
  Despite growing up in Sweden, I didn’t learn how to ski until last winter. I
  was a Chinese immigrant, speaking English, trying to find my place in a
  Swedish school. Every winter, my classmates left for ski trips while I stayed
  behind.
</P>
<P>
  As an adult, I’ve started going back for the things I missed. After the first
  heavy snowfall in November, I went to Åre, a ski resort in northern Sweden.
</P>
<P>
  The chairlifts were shut down due to strong winds, and I ended up on a
  T-bar—something I hadn’t used before. You ride it standing, sharing a bar with
  another skier as it pulls you uphill, tucked under your hips. It works best if
  you’re about the same height.
</P>
<Image
  data={tBarLift}
